From: p5r-proton
Subject: ntdll: allow in-place heap resize for LFH blocks

Persona 5 Royal is CPU bound on the GE-Proton11-12 base (Wine 11) even though the
GPU is mostly idle, and still short of the ~100 FPS title screen baseline of the
old GE-Proton 7 build (Wine 7 / fsync).

Wine 10+ introduced the Low Fragmentation Heap frontend, whose
heap_resize_block_lfh refuses any reallocation that changes the block size and
falls back to allocate + memcpy + free. Wine 7 resized in place within the block,
which made HeapReAlloc cheap for the small-object patterns P5R uses.

Backport the Wine 7 in-place resize semantics: refuse only when the new size does
not fit into the existing block, instead of refusing every resize that changes the
rounded block size.

---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/heap.c	2026-11-04 00:21:57.341339097 +0000
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/heap.c	2026-11-12 22:16:30.227291652 +0000
@@ -2193,9 +2193,10 @@
 
 static NTSTATUS heap_resize_block_lfh( struct block *block, ULONG flags, SIZE_T block_size, SIZE_T size, SIZE_T *old_size, void **ret )
 {
-    /* as native LFH does it with different block size: refuse to resize even though we could */
-    if (ROUND_SIZE( *old_size, BLOCK_ALIGN - 1) != ROUND_SIZE( size, BLOCK_ALIGN - 1)) return STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
-    if (size >= *old_size) return STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
+    /* Wine 7 resized in place within the block; newer LFH refuses unless the
+       block size is unchanged. Backport the Wine 7 behaviour so HeapReAlloc on
+       small objects does not bounce through a fresh allocation. */
+    if (size > (SIZE_T)( block_get_size( block ) - block_get_overhead( block ) )) return STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
 
     block_size = BLOCK_BIN_SIZE( BLOCK_SIZE_BIN( block_size ) );
     block_set_flags( block, BLOCK_FLAG_USER_MASK & ~BLOCK_FLAG_USER_INFO, BLOCK_USER_FLAGS( flags ) );
